    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0649" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p1/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">771.00/10–852: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        France</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d306-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret
                        priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-10-08T15:33:00-05:00">October 8, 1952—3:33
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2017. Dept has decided handle Moroccan item in GA in same manner as Tunisian
                    question. For time being we will follow same line with other UN Dels and press
                    as we are presently following re Tunisia: namely, in reply to inquiries from
                    other dels USUN will inform them in confidence of our position; we will reply to
                    press inquiries that we are consulting with other dels on this and other agenda
                        items.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d306-f2"/></p>
                <p>Pls inform FonOff of foregoing decision which we gather from Hoppenot’s statement
                    will not be surprising to Fr. FYI USUN will commence answering inquiries on Oct
                    10 along above lines.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d306-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d306-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was drafted by Elting (UNP) and McBride (WE) and was cleared with
                    AF. It was repeated to USUN, Rabat, and Tangier.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d306-f2" n="2" xml:id="d306-f2-content">
                <p>For details, see documentation on Tunisia, <ref target="#pg665">pp. 665</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
